</p>  <!-- 7 Ways to Enter Law --> <h2 data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>7 Ways to Enter Law</h2> <p data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>
Before you dive into options, understand the structural, financial, and entry differences between examinations and merit routes.
</p> <div class="table-wrap" data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <table data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <thead data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <tr data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <th data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Pathway</th> <th data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Best For</th> <th data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Key Differentiator</th> <th data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Approx. Fees/Year</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <tr data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s><strong data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>CLAT (National NLUs)</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>High rankers, national career focus</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Single exam for 24 National Law Universities + 60+ affiliated colleges</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>₹2.5L - ₹3.5L</td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s><strong data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>AILET (NLU Delhi)</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Specifically targeting NLU Delhi</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Standalone exam, separate merit list; high corporate firm recruitment advantage</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>₹2.5L - ₹3L</td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s><strong data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>KSLU Merit (Karnataka State)</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>State law practice, budget-conscious</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s><strong data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>No entrance exam!</strong> General admissions are strictly based on PUC/10+2 merit marks</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>₹15K - ₹80K</td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s><strong data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>LSAT India / Private</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Premium private schools, flexible entrance</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Accepted by Jindal Global Law School, Alliance, RV, and 80+ top private colleges</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>₹3L - ₹8L</td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s><strong data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>CUET-UG (Central Univs)</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Targeting Delhi University, BHU, Jamia</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Central government universities via NTA examination</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>₹10K - ₹50K</td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s><strong data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Direct / Management Quota</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Low entrance rank, quick private admission</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Direct entry via high-budget seats in autonomous private colleges</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>₹4L - ₹10L</td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s><strong data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Study Abroad (LLB)</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>High budget, global legal exposure</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Direct LLB programs in UK, Australia, or Canada (requires clearing local bar to return)</td> <td data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>₹15L - ₹40L/year</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> <div class="callout" data-astro-cid-vrm3676s> <div class="callout-label" data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Universal Truth</div> <p data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>
Every pathway leads to a Bar Council of India (BCI) approved degree. The real difference lies in tuition fees, peer network, and initial placement exposure. Focus on matching your budget and career goals, rather than falling into the "NLU-or-nothing" trap.
</p> </div> <!-- 7 Domains --> <h2 data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>Don't pick a law course by "prestige". Pick by what you'll enjoy daily.</h2> <p data-astro-cid-vrm3676s>
